    {"content":"<h1>How to Pass Creativity Techniques</h1><h2>Universidad Europea Creative Campus · UEM 2026-27</h2><p><strong>Rubén Vega Balbás, PhD</strong></p><p><em>6 ECTS · 150 h · 80 h contact · Year 3 · Design</em></p><p>Final event theme: <strong>What is creativity for you?</strong></p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Official weights (unchanged)</h2><table><tr><th>Knowledge tests</th><td>60%</td></tr><tr><th>Delivery / presentation</th><td>40%</td></tr></table><p>Studio choreography below maps onto these instruments — it does not rewrite the guía.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Every session (order binding)</h2><ol><li><strong>Analysis strip</strong> — sessions 1–2: professor models analysis; from session 3: <strong>2 students × 15 min</strong> defence</li><li><strong>Masterclass</strong> — ideas + images</li><li><strong>Lab (Portfolio)</strong> — exercises + debates → portfolio</li><li><strong>Workshop (Deliverable)</strong> — time on the next graded deliverable</li></ol><p><em>Lab ≠ Workshop.</em> Lab leaves traces; Workshop advances deliverables.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Slide rule</h2><p>Before Lab exercises, a <strong>geometrical</strong> slide announces: exercises are coming and they go into your <strong>portfolio index</strong>.</p><p>Workshop open + outro also use geometrical backgrounds. Masterclass content uses course images (accepted media packs).</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Five deliverables</h2><ol><li><strong>D1 Analysis</strong> — 15 min defence · slideshow support · 2 students/session from s3</li><li><strong>D2 Transposition</strong> — free format · discursive circulation / palimpsest (critical review)</li><li><strong>D3 Atrium</strong> — tech script + live defence · theme <em>What is creativity for you?</em></li><li><strong>D4 Portfolio index</strong> — Lab exercises + D1–D3</li><li><strong>D5 Exam</strong> — test/questionnaire + final self-review of process</li></ol>"},
    {"content":"<h2>D1 intra-rubric</h2><table><tr><th>Presentation</th><td>70%</td></tr><tr><th>Deliverable support</th><td>20%</td></tr><tr><th>Peer debate</th><td>10%</td></tr></table><p>Polish alone fails. Defend choices, criteria, and what you discarded.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Ordinary / extraordinary</h2><p>Binding dates: official UEM guide + Campus Virtual. Failed evidence is repaired by defined resubmission, not attendance.</p>","calendar_note":true},
